  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ESY-MAP Workshop on Environmental and Social Assessment for Hydrogen Projects in Morocco - venue and catering</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity supported a two-day ESY-MAP workshop in Morocco to analyse the country&apos;s Environmental and Social Impact Assessment (ESIA) and Strategic Environmental Assessment (SEA) systems for renewable energy projects, with a focus on green hydrogen.The workshop brought together stakeholders from government, academia and civil society and contributes to the objectives of the Netherlands-Morocco Memorandum of Understanding on sustainable energy cooperation.Using the ESY-MAP diagnostic tool, participants assessed legislative frameworks, institutional capacity and assessment practices, and identified priority actions to strengthen environmental and social assessment processes for hydrogen projects.CERF funding supported the venue and catering, enabling an effective setting for dialogue and stakeholder engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
